            <ArticleTitle>Back to the roots of regulated necrosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>303-304</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1083/jcb.201612078</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In recent years, our knowledge of how cells die by regulated pathways of necrosis has increased tremendously. In this issue, Distéfano et al. (2017. J. Cell Biol. https://doi.org/10.1083/jcb.201605110) provide yet another milestone in our understanding of regulated necrosis as they identify a ferroptosis-like cell death in Arabidopsis thaliana.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 Todorov and Linkermann.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
